S.B. 204
Physical Therapy Payment Amendments
House Amendments Amendment 1 March 04, 2026 08:47 AM
Representative David Shallenberger proposes the following amendments:
1. Line 34 through 42:
34 shall permit an insured to select a participating provider who is a physical therapist to
35 provide physical therapy services.
36 (3)
(a) An accident and health insurance policy that provides coverage for physical therapy
37 services may not impose a copayment, coinsurance, or office visit deductible for a
38 covered physical therapy visit that exceeds the copayment, coinsurance, or office visit
39 deductible applicable to a visit with a primary care provider.
(b) Subsection (3)(a) applies to a health benefit plan renewed or entered into on or after
January 1, 2027.
40 [(3)](4) An accident and health insurance policy shall clearly state in literature explaining
41 the policy the options available to insureds under Subsections (1) and (2).
42 [(4)](5) An accident and health insurance policy may not impose a higher premium, higher
